# A boolean that may stay empty, read as a condition — refused

`hoog` is defined only when `pas_toe` holds. Catala raises "no applicable rule
to define this variable" when the exception reads `hoog` and `pas_toe` is
false, while the IR reads the characteristic as not held and the base
decides. The plugin refuses the condition read of `hoog`. Own-authored,
rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope Aanslag:
  input pas_toe content boolean
  input grens content integer
  internal hoog content boolean
  output heffing content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition hoog under condition pas_toe consequence equals grens > 10
  definition heffing equals 1
  exception definition heffing under condition hoog consequence equals 2
```
